From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mindone <mindone@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] satellite: resolve support as false without a vendor service

When config_satellite_service_package is empty, SatelliteModemInterface
stops binding for good, every requestIsSatelliteSupported() ends with
SATELLITE_RESULT_RADIO_NOT_AVAILABLE and mIsSatelliteSupported stays
null, so updateSatelliteSupportedState() never runs and
mSatelliteSessionController is never created. ServiceStateTracker then
retries registerForSatelliteModemStateChanged() from pollStateDone() and
updateCarrierDisplayName() on every poll, and each attempt logs two
errors.

The package name is static device configuration (bindService() stops its
retries for the same reason), so a device without it does not support
OEM satellite. Resolve that once on the controller's handler after the
singleton is published: the session controller is created in its
unsupported state, listeners register normally and requests are answered
from the cached value. setSatelliteServicePackageName() still clears the
cached state when a test service is installed.

---
diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/satellite/SatelliteController.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/satellite/SatelliteController.java
index 63e22c9..7947fe3 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/satellite/SatelliteController.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/satellite/SatelliteController.java
@@ -1014,9 +1014,19 @@ public class SatelliteController extends Handler {
         if (sInstance == null) {
             sInstance = new SatelliteController(
                     context, WorkerThread.get().getLooper(), featureFlags);
+            sInstance.post(sInstance::resolveSupportWithoutVendorService);
         }
     }
 
+    private void resolveSupportWithoutVendorService() {
+        if (getIsSatelliteSupported() != null
+                || mSatelliteModemInterface.isSatelliteServiceSupported()) {
+            return;
+        }
+        plogd("resolveSupportWithoutVendorService: no satellite vendor service is configured");
+        updateSatelliteSupportedState(false);
+    }
+
     /**
      * Create a SatelliteController to act as a backend service of
      * {@link android.telephony.satellite.SatelliteManager}
